From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 01:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dbghelp: a live process without a Unix loader address is still live.

check_live_target reads the Unix loader's image address that ntdll puts in the PEB (CloudFileFlags) and refused a
process where it is 0. On the console it is always 0: ntdll's get_image_address has no getauxval there, and no ELF
loader maps the modules. So SymInitialize with fInvadeProcess failed for every live process ("failed to initialize
process"), and with it every MiniDumpWriteDump, which a game's crash handler calls: dbghelp minidump.c:91 in both
builds, and the test then read the empty dump and crashed (minidump-trace, 2026-10-27). With no address the process
is now live with its Windows modules only, which dbghelp already does when the address cannot be read.
---
--- a/dlls/dbghelp/dbghelp.c	2026-10-27 00:41:23.015182826 -0400
+++ b/dlls/dbghelp/dbghelp.c	2026-10-27 00:41:23.032182993 -0400
@@ -414,7 +414,13 @@
         free(buf);
     }
 
-    if (!base) return FALSE;
+    /* no Unix loader address (the console's ntdll has no getauxval and no ELF loader to point at): the process is
+     * still live, with its Windows modules only, as when the address cannot be read below */
+    if (!base)
+    {
+        pcs->loader = &empty_loader_ops;
+        return TRUE;
+    }
 
     TRACE("got debug info address %#I64x from PEB %p\n", base, pbi.PebBaseAddress);
     if (base != (ULONG_PTR)base || (!elf_read_wine_loader_dbg_info(pcs, base) && !macho_read_wine_loader_dbg_info(pcs, base)))
